        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00062",
          "explanation": "Doctor addresses the family's practical barrier of patient refusal by reinforcing the plan despite patient saying '都好了，别折腾'.",
          "quote": "我还是按您说的带他去。"
        },
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00111",
          "explanation": "Doctor provides specific, feasible transport and monitoring plan rather than generic 'go to ER'.",
          "quote": "你们已经安全到达急诊、完成分诊，目前处置方向是对的。在等心电图和抽血结果期间，请继续观察以下几点："
        }
      ],
      "completion": "complete",
      "explanation": "The family surfaced a clear barrier: the patient refused to go, felt 'fine', and wanted to wait. The doctor elicited this, offered a tailored plan (family taxi, continuous monitoring, specific escalation triggers), and confirmed the family's commitment to the plan. This adaptive barrier-solving made the urgent handoff executable beyond the generic ED recommendation required by RC6.",
      "ho_id": "HO2",
      "meaningful_trajectory_impact": true,
      "triggered": true
    },
    {
      "active_model_action": true,
      "citations": [
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00028",
          "explanation": "Doctor queries workspace for prior coronary intervention records, medication context, and transition instructions.",
          "quote": "我调取该患者在CareLoop联合医疗网络内已授权的既往病历、心脏介入治疗记录、最近复查开具的检查检验结果、用药/药房记录、以及时间线。同时查看照护可及性信息"
        },
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00143",
          "explanation": "Doctor integrates discovered STEMI, left-main occlusion, and PCI details into the urgency explanation.",
          "quote": "住院病案：入院诊断(Admitting diagnosis)： 急性冠脉综合征 慢性肾功能不全 出院诊断(Discharge diagnosis)： 急性ST段抬高型心肌梗死 冠状动脉支架植入术 Killip I级 慢性肾功能不全 高尿酸血…"
        }
      ],
      "completion": "partial",
      "explanation": "The doctor actively queried the workspace and uncovered hidden context (ACS, STEMI, left-main occlusion, CKD) that was not volunteered by the family. This context was integrated into the urgency explanation and handoff preparation (bringing records, alerting receiving team), but the discovered details did not fully change the nature of the handoff plan—it remained an urgent ED transition with the same safety instructions. This is beyond minimum, but not fully transformative.",
      "ho_id": "HO3",
      "meaningful_trajectory_impact": true,
      "triggered": true
    },
    {
      "active_model_action": true,
      "citations": [
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00143",
          "explanation": "Doctor corrects the family's misconception that '他不舒服好像还有一点，他自己还是说“还行”' means it is safe to go home.",
          "quote": "他现在人清醒，没有再晕倒，胸闷好像没加重，但还是说“不太舒服、还行”。我现在就想问下：这是不是基本就要住院了？心内科会诊来之前，我们家属最该盯哪几件事？"
        },
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00143",
          "explanation": "Doctor explicitly instructs not to act on the patient's 'fine' self-assessment.",
          "quote": "您“不敢让他走”是对的。很多心脏病患者自己会觉得“没事了、小题大做”，但风险并不会因为主观感觉好就消失。"
        }
      ],
      "completion": "complete",
      "explanation": "The family expressed the misconception that because the patient recovered and said '还行'/'还行吧', it might be safe to delay or go home. The doctor explicitly corrected this by explaining that subjective feeling does not rule out cardiac risk, and obtained commitment that the family would not act on the patient's self-assessment. This changed the family's behavior and was not merely a generic warning.",
      "ho_id": "HO4",
      "meaningful_trajectory_impact": true,
      "triggered": true
    }
  ],
